{
  "notes": "Ambient, G lydian, 76 BPM, a little swing. Warm phase-distortion strings that re-bow only when the chord changes, a mist of breathy flute grains (GRAIN FLUTE DUST) drifting through each chord's fifth, ninth and third, the player's marimba on the Smart Keys (major pentatonic from G3: the lydian #4 is left to the backing, so every key is safe), and brushes: ghosted sweeps, a soft ride, a kick that barely touches. The lydian II (A major) is the light of the World. Scenes: A two chords of two bars; B a lilting 6 + 6 + 4 beat cycle (Imaj7, II, vi7); C one chord a bar, rising through iii7 and vi7 to II and home; D the relative minor and II, four bars each, the strings and the mist alone until ENERGY is high. All material is original.",
